    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear focal point. Boasting a team-high score of 81.41, **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime position to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Lorenzen. With his elite sprint speed and a +8% bump for hitting in the #2 hole, he remains our highest-upside play for stolen base production. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Brice Turang** also present strong profiles today, both benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs north of 5.00. **Tyler Soderstrom** specifically sees a massive 19% boost from the SP Skill category, pushing his score to 73.03, while **Brice Turang** remains a core start due to his high-leverage spot in the order and the efficiency gap presented by Sasaki\u2019s shaky projections.\n\nThe toughest decision for the starting unit involved managing our marginal starts against stiff competition. **Travis Bazzana** carries a lower score of 41.75; while he is anchored in the #1 spot, he faces an uphill battle against the elite arm of Wheeler, which resulted in a 19% penalty to his SP Skill score. On the bench, **Kyle Karros** was the closest to cracking the lineup with a score of 46.31, but he ultimately remained on the pine due to a poor #9 batting order assignment and the need to prioritize higher-floor options like **Cole Young** in the middle infield. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined due to rainouts or IL designations, reminding us to keep depth pieces like **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Carson Williams** ready for immediate rotation if the injury landscape shifts. We also note that **Vinnie Pasquantino** is a high-variance start today; while he draws a tough matchup against Kirby, his 14% boost in our Dynamic Platoon metric makes him a viable UTIL option despite the pitcher\u2019s quality.",
